cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the software. It accompanies the
  article "Can a published CF-LIBS quantification be reconstructed? A
  reproducibility-audit framework and reporting checklist" by Homa
  Saeidfirozeh and Martin Ferus.
title: >-
  CF-LIBS Reproducibility Audit: an executable A1-A5 audit engine for
  CF-LIBS/LIPS quantification
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-07
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Saeidfirozeh
    given-names: Homa
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6687-1496"
    affiliation: >-
      J. Heyrovský Institute of Physical Chemistry, Czech Academy of Sciences
repository-code: "https://github.com/homasf/cf-libs-repro-audit"
url: "https://github.com/homasf/cf-libs-repro-audit"
abstract: >-
  An executable, paper-independent A1-A5 reproducibility-audit engine for
  testing whether quantitative CF-LIBS/LIPS calculation chains can be
  reconstructed from values printed in a publication. The software produces
  deterministic validation, linewidth, scale, invertibility and reporting
  checks and includes a worked example with automated tests.
keywords:
  - CF-LIBS
  - LIPS
  - reproducibility
  - spectroscopy
  - metrology
  - Stark broadening
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Can a published CF-LIBS quantification be reconstructed? A
      reproducibility-audit framework and reporting checklist
    authors:
      - family-names: Saeidfirozeh
        given-names: Homa
      - family-names: Ferus
        given-names: Martin
    year: 2026
